---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About node-opcua — the open-source OPC UA stack for Node.js.">
  <section class="about-content">
    <h1>About node-opcua</h1>

    <p>
      <strong>node-opcua</strong> is the most popular open-source OPC UA stack for
      Node.js, JavaScript, and TypeScript. It has been in continuous development
      since 2014 and is used in production at Mercedes-Benz, Renault, Siemens,
      and hundreds of industrial deployments worldwide.
    </p>

    <h2>What is OPC UA?</h2>
    <p>
      OPC Unified Architecture (OPC UA) is the industrial interoperability
      standard for secure, reliable data exchange between devices, controllers,
      and enterprise systems. It is platform-independent and maintained by the
      OPC Foundation.
    </p>

    <h2>The project</h2>
    <p>
      node-opcua provides a full client and server SDK that lets developers
      build OPC UA applications in JavaScript and TypeScript. The stack supports
      security, subscriptions, historical access, alarms and conditions, and
      the full OPC UA information model.
    </p>

    <h2>The team</h2>
    <p>
      node-opcua is maintained primarily by Etienne Rossignon at
      <a href="https://www.sterfive.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sterfive SAS</a>,
      a French company specializing in OPC UA consulting and commercial support.
    </p>

    <h2>License</h2>
    <p>
      node-opcua is released under the MIT license. Commercial modules with
      extended functionality are available through Sterfive.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-content {
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-section, 4.5rem) 1.5rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  p {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
